\subsection{The extended friends: where this account stands}
\label{sec:wf-ewf}

The dissolution just given does not stand alone; it stands in a crowded and
recently theorem-rich field, and the field's results locate it precisely. A
programme of \emph{extended} Wigner's friend arguments has turned the thought
experiment into no-go theorems: Brukner's no-go for observer-independent facts
\autocite{brukner2018nogo}; the Frauchiger--Renner argument that inferences
chained across nested observers yield contradiction \autocite{Frauchiger_2018};
and, sharpest, the Local Friendliness theorem, which from the conjunction of
\emph{absoluteness of observed events} and \emph{local agency} alone derives
inequalities strictly weaker than Bell's, so that their quantum violation bounds
reality more tightly than Bell's theorem does
\autocite{bong2020strong,cavalcantiwiseman2021implications}. Both Brukner's
inequality and the Local Friendliness inequalities have been violated in
proof-of-principle photonic experiments
\autocite{proietti2019experimental,bong2020strong}, and the assumptions have
since been pushed weaker still
\autocite{haddaracavalcanti2023possibilistic,morenoetal2022maximally}. A recent
review unifies six such arguments and reaches two conclusions this section could
have written \autocite{schmidyingleifer2023sixewf}: every argument hinges on
assumptions about correlations between outcomes that are not accessible to any
observer even in principle, and the most defensible reading of the strongest
theorems is that measurement outcomes are perspectival rather than absolute.

The framework's location in that assumption space is exact, and it is derived
rather than chosen. Local agency is kept untouched. Absoluteness of observed
events --- whose intended meaning has itself been carefully dissected
\autocite{adlam2024nonabsoluteness} --- is in this account a \emph{grade}, never
a threshold: an observed event is absolute to the degree that its record is
redundantly copied (\S\ref{sec:wf-redundancy}), so the low-redundancy violations
the theorems exhibit are the framework's expectation, not its embarrassment.
And the Frauchiger--Renner consistency assumption --- that an inference
conditioned on an outcome may be chained across agents --- is restricted, not
rejected: it holds along records that persist to the comparison, and fails
exactly where the protocol un-copies the record it conditions on. This
discharges the promise made in \S\ref{sec:self-reference}. The contradiction is
manufactured by transporting a conditional through an un-done \textsc{fanout}:
the antecedent's record has been recovered into the fibre and no longer exists
at the base, so the inference has no carrier
(Proposition~\ref{prop:f1-dictionary}); in the language of
\S\ref{sec:self-reference}, the undone measurement is an anti-event, and the
conditional's content has returned to the signed, pre-record regime where it can
cancel. Nurgalieva and Renner's epistemic-logic diagnosis --- the multi-agent
trust axiom fails when memories are manipulated
\autocite{nurgalievarenner2020testing} --- is the same restriction stated in
logic; the geometry says why. The review's diagnostic lands the same way: the
correlations every argument needs are correlations with records that cannot
coexist, and the framework does not merely render such quantities inaccessible
--- it declines to define them at the base at all.

The graded reading, meanwhile, is ceasing to be a theorist's option and becoming
the field's experimental variable. The ``thoughtful'' reformulation of Local
Friendliness makes observerhood the open question and names its target
experiment --- a reversible artificial agent on a quantum computer
\autocite{wisemancavalcantirieffel2023thoughtful} --- and a first programme now
runs extended-friend circuits on present-day processors, proposing a ``branch
factor'' to quantify observerness, demonstrating violations at branch factor
sixteen, and asking outright what the branch factor of a detector, an eye, a
brain would be \autocite{russozeng2025branch}. The branch factor is a
laboratory-internal instance of this section's redundancy parameter, measured on
the same class of hardware as this paper's own executed circuits
(Appendix~\ref{app:hw-ckm}); what the framework supplies is what the programme's
shape presupposes --- violations available wherever the un-copying is actually
performable, difficulty and Landauer cost growing with $R$, absoluteness only as
the limit. The exposed commitment is the gradedness itself: a demonstrated sharp
threshold --- an observer class at which violations vanish discontinuously while
reversal remains performable --- would refute the redundancy reading, and no
such evidence exists. The theorems have their sceptics, who argue they constrain
less than advertised \autocite{okon2025reassessing}, and relative-facts
positions have been pressed hard in the recent literature
\autocite{lawrencemarkiewiczzukowski2023relative}; nothing here is recruited
from the theorems --- the denial of low-$R$ absoluteness is derived from the
framework's own machinery --- and the reconciliation of
\S\ref{sec:wf-reconciliation}, that the two charts agree on everything both can
check, is the answer this account gives where the pressing is hardest.

One absence in this literature is worth recording, because the next subsection
fills it. The extended arguments lengthen the chain of observers to strengthen
their theorems, and treat every added observer as interchangeable with the last;
nowhere in the field is it asked whether the chain itself has structure ---
which rung an observer occupies is never permitted to matter. The algebra, the
next subsection shows, disagrees: it matters exactly once more, and then never
again.

% SPLICE-END wf-ewf 2026-08-30
